{"availability":"available","full":"kaspermarstal/plprql","name":"plprql","description":"Use PRQL in PostgreSQL","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":476,"forks":5,"created":"2023-09-15T23:13:05Z","updated":"2026-09-28T09:30:32Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://prql-lang.org/","topics":["extension","pgrx","postgresql","prql","sql"],"demo":"https://prql-lang.org/playground/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:44.723Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:44.723Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:44.723Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T09:01:44.723Z","stars":476,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["PL/PRQL is a PostgreSQL extension that lets you write stored procedures with PRQL. The extension supports PostgreSQL v13-18 on Linux and macOS.","PRQL (Pipelined Relational Query Language) is an open source query language for data manipulation and analysis that compiles to SQL. PRQL introduces a pipeline concept similar to Unix pipes that transforms data line-by-line. The sequential series of transformations reduces the complexity often encountered with nested SQL queries and makes your data manipulation logic easier to read and write. With PL/PRQL you can write Procedural Language (PL) functions with PRQL instead of the traditional PL/pgSQL, combining the simplicity of PRQL with the power of stored procedures."],"features":["Write functions with PRQL - Useful for large analytical queries","Compile PRQL queries to SQL queries - Useful for development and debugging","Execute PRQL queries - Useful for prototyping and custom queries in ORMs","For more information on the design of the extension, see the design document.","For more information on PRQL, visit the PRQL website, playground or repository."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kaspermarstal/plprql/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8fe872197f329a0e3103e9756e68328987ab1dab65ce72f3d7b83d24020be50b","extr